			"Message": "docs(Echo): Add Shim Compatibility section to Architecture.md\n\nDocument the deep-shim interception system integration point for Echo. The new section describes the dual-tier shim architecture:\n\n- **🟠 Low-Level Shim (TierShim=Own|Preempt)** — Engine prototype hooks for Error, Emitter, Cancel, Dispose, Async, and Timing interception\n- **🔵 Coverage Shim (TierShim=Proxy|Replace)** — Application-level IPC SwallowMap, DI proxy, and AuditLog routing\n\nEcho itself carries no shim-specific modules; shim events are routed through Wind, Mountain, and Cocoon. The feature is gated behind the `TierShim` environment variable (default: `None` ensuring zero overhead).",
			"SHA": "c3226f386b6d7a5b1aa7a77b10c5cd4137e61d81"
